From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the S_PWM controller

The A733 has a third PWM controller in the CPUS domain, S_PWM, which the
device tree does not describe. Add it as r_pwm, disabled, and one pin
group for each pin that carries an S_PWM output on the Radxa Cubie A7S
header or its LED. The values (page numbers are pages of the A733
manual PDF):

- Registers at 0x07023000, 4 KiB in the memory map (p.29). The manual
  gives the registers as those of PWM0 (section 18.7.7, p.1332), whose
  last register is at 0x364, so the size is 0x400 as for PWM0 and PWM1.
  The channel distance is the A733 one the compatible selects.
- Ten channels: S_PWM0_[9:0] (section 18.7.1, p.1322).
- Interrupt 239, which is GIC_SPI 207 (section 12.2.3.1, p.620).
- Clocks, all in the PRCM: the bus gate S_PWM_GATING and the reset
  S_PWM_RST in S_PWM_BGR_REG (section 4.2.5.11, p.245) and the module
  clock S_PWM_CLK in S_PWM_CLK_REG (section 4.2.5.10, p.244), with its
  gate and a source of DCXO, RTC_32K, RC16M or SYS_CLK24M (sections
  18.7.3 and 18.7.5.1, p.1323 to 1324). There is no other gate on the
  register path, so the node holds all three. The module clock is the
  hosc input of the driver and the APB0 clock of the CPUS domain its apb
  input; the manual does not say which clock the second source of the
  clock configuration register selects for S_PWM.
- S-PWM0-n on function 6 of PL2 to PL11 and PM0 to PM5 (tables 18-38
  and 18-39, p.1582 to 1583; PL_CFG0 p.1813, PM_CFG0 p.1821 to 1822).
  PL5, PL6 and PL7 (S-PWM0-3, -4 and -5) are connected to the header
  J11, PM3 and PM4 (S-PWM0-5 and -0) to the header J6 (schematic V1.10,
  sheet 14), PM2 (S-PWM0-4) to the green LED (sheet 16).

The node stays disabled and the pin groups are /omit-if-no-ref/,
because nothing fitted on the board uses them. The green LED stays a
GPIO LED.

Not covered: enabling the controller on the board and the pins of the
bank that are not on the header.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with the node enabled for a test on PM2, the
channel ran the period and duty cycle set through sysfs from the module
clock, and its interrupt status raised the interrupt; the LED was not
watched.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 55 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index a203e4af921f..36f730e32d63 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1697,6 +1697,19 @@ r_wdt: watchdog@7021000 {
 			clock-names = "hosc", "losc";
 		};
 
+		r_pwm: pwm@7023000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm";
+			reg = <0x07023000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 207 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_PWM>, <&r_ccu CLK_R_PWM>,
+				 <&r_ccu CLK_R_APB0>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "hosc", "apb";
+			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_PWM>;
+			#pwm-cells = <3>;
+			allwinner,npwms = <10>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		r_pio: pinctrl@7025000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-pinctrl";
 			reg = <0x07025000 0x410>;
@@ -1731,6 +1744,48 @@ r_ir_rx_pl6_pin: r-ir-rx-pl6-pin {
 				allwinner,pinmux = <5>;
 				function = "s_cir_rx";
 			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pl5_pin: r-pwm-pl5-pin {
+				pins = "PL5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pl6_pin: r-pwm-pl6-pin {
+				pins = "PL6";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pl7_pin: r-pwm-pl7-pin {
+				pins = "PL7";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pm2_pin: r-pwm-pm2-pin {
+				pins = "PM2";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pm3_pin: r-pwm-pm3-pin {
+				pins = "PM3";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
+
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_pwm_pm4_pin: r-pwm-pm4-pin {
+				pins = "PM4";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <6>;
+				function = "s_pwm0";
+			};
 		};
 
 		r_ir: ir@7040000 {
